A corrected, robust useCollectionDrag.ts

This version:

Does not use long-press timers

Starts drag after a small “slop” (5–8px) to avoid accidental drags

Locks the scroll container during an active drag (belt-and-suspenders)

Uses native PointerEvent only, no async synthetic event usage

Cleans up reliably


> It also assumes you can pass a ref to the scrollable container (recommended). If you cannot pass a ref, you can still keep the touch-action fix and remove the scroll-lock bits.



